{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender metaball objects blender metaball objects","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md","fileName":"Blender Metaball Objects.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Metaball Objects","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects]] · [[Blender Scene Object Types]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects","Blender Scene Object Types","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender metaball objects blender metaball objects","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md","fileName":"Blender Metaball Objects.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Metaball Objects","heading":"Blender Metaball Objects","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Metaballs are implicit surfaces whose elements merge as they approach one another, resembling droplets joining into a larger drop. Their influence can also be subtractive, cutting into another metaball surface.\n\nBecause the blended surface updates as elements move, metaballs are useful for fluid, organic, or rapidly changing forms. The artist controls when elements combine and how strongly each contributes to the shared surface.\n\nMetaballs belong to their own Blender object type rather than being ordinary mesh components. Their implicit field can later be converted when a production pipeline requires explicit polygon topology for editing or export.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects","Blender Scene Object Types","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender metaball objects blender metaball objects","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Metaball Objects.md","fileName":"Blender Metaball Objects.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Metaball Objects","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf]]\n\n[[creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Sculpting and Geometry Objects","Blender Scene Object Types","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","creatinggameenvironmentsinblender3d.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}